                    {
                        "translation_id": "0d2cd3d3-fcb5-4e13-9e9a-1223e992616a",
                        "source_entry_id": "9bd25e7d-5863-330e-9dbf-caaac66eac01",
                        "source_sense_id": "7c4b0fb6-c679-3600-b70c-e36ff92b9b73",
                        "target_lang_word": "pent",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03799aeb-05d5-387c-8955-2b4baa4f986a",
                                        "entry_id": "3928e1d8-d613-38ac-ba83-f3359133504f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Confinement; concealment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a024838-69c4-4442-bb57-c4b5f39170cf",
                                                "sense_id": "03799aeb-05d5-387c-8955-2b4baa4f986a",
                                                "text": "There was a catch in my voice, thick as it was with the pent of unshed tears; had I let them flow they would have come out forty per cent proof."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "pent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "73233094-d045-3a85-83a0-3ece67e6c76b",
                                        "entry_id": "1450070e-d429-38fb-a0ad-ff5d01d5c98d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Confined in, or as if in, a pen; imprisoned."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3cf3a415-7c7f-49e7-b409-be42b1343eec",
                                                "sense_id": "73233094-d045-3a85-83a0-3ece67e6c76b",
                                                "text": "As the old woman, with a gigantic and distorted image of herself thrown half upon the wall behind her, half upon the roof above, sat bending over the few loose bricks within which it was pent, on the damp hearth of the chimney—for there was no stove—she looked as if she were watching at some witch’s altar for a favourable token; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a1d0772-c988-4dc7-b5a5-7e2da4d8ab73",
                                                "sense_id": "73233094-d045-3a85-83a0-3ece67e6c76b",
                                                "text": "Wherever Miss Clavering went, this infatuated young fellow continued to follow her; and being aware that his engagement to his cousin was known in the world, he was forced to make a mystery of his passion, and confine it to his own breast, so that it was so pent in there and pressed down, that it is a wonder he did not explode some day with the stormy secret, and perish collapsed after the outburst."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db5be83f-33ab-48ba-8978-fb0652c0ecc1",
                                                "sense_id": "73233094-d045-3a85-83a0-3ece67e6c76b",
                                                "text": "My object all sublime\nI shall achieve in time —\nTo let the punishment fit the crime —\nThe punishment fit the crime;\nAnd make each prisoner pent\nUnwillingly represent\nA source of innocent merriment!\nOf innocent merriment!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "948c6331-c809-4ba0-b4e6-94799afce270",
                                                "sense_id": "73233094-d045-3a85-83a0-3ece67e6c76b",
                                                "text": "Numa, ravenous with hunger, had long since learned the futility of roaring and moaning as he searched for prey, but now that it was as surely his as though already he had felt the soft flesh beneath his still mighty paw, he opened his huge jaws, and gave vent to his long-pent rage in a series of deafening roars that made the air tremble."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "pent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f6230a9a-2825-3de9-b49c-193d35b0a45e",
                                        "entry_id": "3c1c6a13-e229-3b43-bb5d-491b78e58f42",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "simple past and past participle of pen; alternative form of penned."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "form-of",
                                            "participle",
                                            "past"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "pent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b5b8483-a97b-3f5a-a1e2-d95a23f0043d",
                                        "entry_id": "b4a8dc3f-c538-325c-899a-1d1d3991b922",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pentatonic scale."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4629def-4fcc-49e7-b8f4-ae5c7cfadd2f",
                                                "sense_id": "4b5b8483-a97b-3f5a-a1e2-d95a23f0043d",
                                                "text": "The major pent is the same minor pent pattern only shifted down 3 frets toward the nut. Like John B told me for Sunshine of your love. Play Bm and then Dm pent and it will sound good. He also pointed out that Bm pent includes the same exact notes as DM pent. So the idea is if the song is in D, try both minor and major pents and see how it works."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "pent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3922aef5-05dd-3f04-b6f1-fa2e8850e8aa",
                                        "entry_id": "3d154a7f-edf6-348c-b27d-9501f6157e8e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pentacle or pentagram."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd96cee6-3cc5-4c57-b883-4105debb171a",
                                                "sense_id": "3922aef5-05dd-3f04-b6f1-fa2e8850e8aa",
                                                "text": "[> What symbols mean the most to you? For instance, what do you wear around your neck and why?]\nUsually, a triquetra, although I have ankhs, pents and a spell-bottle on amber beads which I wear if I find it necessary to be *really* annoying :)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "54f33bae-eb9d-4a80-a889-afc757cb48a0",
                        "source_entry_id": "9bd25e7d-5863-330e-9dbf-caaac66eac01",
                        "source_sense_id": "7c4b0fb6-c679-3600-b70c-e36ff92b9b73",
                        "target_lang_word": "penthouse",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "penthouse",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "24811c31-7d5e-3605-b767-4c0888ccf90b",
                                        "entry_id": "53703889-add9-39cc-8a2b-cd465c9f7309",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A structure or annexe (especially one with a sloping roof) extending from the side of a building, sometimes as protection from the weather."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0304c1d-6f13-4535-b200-77f61aad99c6",
                                                "sense_id": "24811c31-7d5e-3605-b767-4c0888ccf90b",
                                                "text": "At length, recommending himself to God, he let go one end of his cord, and suffered himself to fall down upon an old shed or penthouse, which, with the weight of his body, fell in with great noise."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e434fa3f-687b-35c4-849b-47ebb2325c31",
                                        "entry_id": "53703889-add9-39cc-8a2b-cd465c9f7309",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something forming a shelter or canopy over something; an awning, shelter, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31a09ef4-0fa7-4623-bdc6-e2c8f6d9ae54",
                                                "sense_id": "e434fa3f-687b-35c4-849b-47ebb2325c31",
                                                "text": "The proboscis […] is doubled up by means of the joint, and in that position lies secure under a scaly penthouse."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2abbc87c-4523-3dbc-be8a-5293a99ef466",
                                        "entry_id": "53703889-add9-39cc-8a2b-cd465c9f7309",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of the sloping roofs at the side of a real tennis court."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca91b8d1-42cd-4cb8-a298-8abc83bb8e98",
                                                "sense_id": "2abbc87c-4523-3dbc-be8a-5293a99ef466",
                                                "text": "2005, Tony Collins (ed.), Encyclopaedia of Traditional British Rural Sports, Routledge, page 262,\nAn odd derivative of real tennis lasted until the latter part of the eighteenth century at Rattray in Perthshire. It was played in the churchyard by two pairs of men, and the method for starting the play was to throw the ball onto the church roof, using it like the sloping penthouse of the tennis court."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5405273f-6e37-3f4a-91cc-a9a7d93eb291",
                                        "entry_id": "53703889-add9-39cc-8a2b-cd465c9f7309",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An apartment or suite found on an upper floor, or floors, of a tall building, especially one that is expensive or luxurious with panoramic views."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f65bfb5-6b4d-451f-ae51-efdf3d2f30a9",
                                                "sense_id": "5405273f-6e37-3f4a-91cc-a9a7d93eb291",
                                                "text": "Night of January 16th is the story of a woman on trial for pushing her wealthy boss-lover from a Manhattan penthouse."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "penthouse",
